ounts as a DiseaseClass term since it names a family of muscle disorders. I'm also going through other candidate terms like \"fibrosis,\" \"fibre degeneration,\" \"pathological features,\" and \"DM pathology,\" deciding these are process descriptions rather than disease mentions and should be skipped, while still weighing whether \"Myotonic dystrophy\" itself should get the DiseaseClass tag given its subtypes DM1 and DM2.\n\nNow I'm compiling the final annotation list with character offsets for each disease mention -- \"myopathy,\" \"Myotonic dystrophy,\" \"DM,\" \"autosomal dominant disorder,\" and repeated DM references -- matching each to the appropriate entity type and guideline section, then assembling everything into a single-line JSON output with rationales for each span.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":84,\"end\":92,\"text\":\"myopathy\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Myopathy refers to a family of muscle diseases rather than one specific disease, so it is a Disease Class mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Disease Class)\"},{\"start\":94,\"end\":112,\"text\":\"Myotonic dystrophy\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Full name of a specific disease, described as an autosomal dominant disorder caused by a CTG repeat expansion. It is a disease name, not the gene or protein name.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions\"},{\"start\":115,\"end\":117,\"text\":\"DM\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Abbreviation for myotonic dystrophy introduced in parentheses. Abbreviation and long form are annotated as separate mentions, and this one refers to the specific disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"6. Annotate all synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":126,\"end\":153,\"text\":\"autosomal dominant disorder\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Describes a family of diseases defined by their inheritance pattern, analogous to the